--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/CACHE-HISTORY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,78 @@
+# Cache history (Hermes strata-030)
+
+Where the SavedState / conversation-cache behaviour came from, and why the code is shaped
+this way. Invariant explanations live next to the code; this file holds only the history.
+
+## Origin of this refactor
+
+A readability review of the cache code arrived via the user from ChatGPT (2026-10-01).
+Claude scoped it, and the work split as BRIEF CELL-C: Muse-1 (engine + cache units),
+Muse-2 (serve cache protocol), reviewed by Sol. Rule throughout: no behaviour change —
+same restore decisions, logs, disk schema (v3) and CLI flags, with the CPU suites
+(`saved_state`, layout, `restore`, `root_disk_codec`, server/keeper) green after every step.
+
+## Earlier cache work (DESIGN-HERMES-CACHE.md)
+
+- **Store policy (E1).** Pinned roots (fixed-prefix ends, never evicted by traffic), byte-budget
+  LRU tips (one recent line tip in host RAM for alternation and forks), and the untouched
+  upstream live chain. Aux (title/side) requests never insert, evict, or advance the clock.
+  A stage-layout change clears the store rather than risk a cross-layout restore. Snapshot
+  capture pins roots and flushes tips with exact emitted boundaries.
+- **Restore (E2).** Longest prefix wins over exact full ids + image/cvec identity; geometry,
+  payload sizes, pointers, capacities and the drafter window are validated before any GPU
+  mutation. Boundary cell k-1 is re-paired from the resume suffix before the suffix prefill
+  (E2b boundary repair).
+- **Disk (E3, schema v3).** Versioned bounded binary codec with trailing checksum, streaming
+  metadata-only startup scan, lazy payload loads, background writer with atomic temp->rename
+  publishing, mtime-LRU trim over recognized files only, and index repair on load failure.
+- **Stats (E4), tests (E5), serve surface.** Per-request source/k/suffix/timings; a dedicated
+  CPU policy suite; aux gating (S1) and the cache inventory API (S2).
+
+## Old review labels and what they required
+
+Sol review / finding / blocker labels marked the rationale behind the strictest checks:
+
+- **Validation before mutation.** Every geometry scalar, KV/indexer size, pointer, capacity
+  and drafter-window bound is proven before any GPU write, so a truncated or corrupt
+  payload fails closed instead of landing half-uploaded.
+- **Window/boundary discipline.** A candidate whose drafter window reaches below the
+  snapshot's first real pair is rejected outright; the boundary cell is always re-paired
+  from the resume suffix, never trusted from speculative rows.
+- **Optional-allocation containment.** Captures, stashes and queue insertions that can
+  allocate must never fail the request they serve: a failed stash only drops that
+  snapshot, and a failed enqueue never suppresses the RAM insert.
+- **Coherence reset.** After a failed mount, repair, or throw during mount, all stages
+  reset and live/chain candidacy dies; a failed reset has no coherent fallback and fails the
+  request outright. Phase-1 load/validation/index-drop exceptions instead keep the index
+  and the chain with no GPU reset (nothing was written yet).
+
+## Fixes that shaped the invariants
+
+- **Fall-through restore (F1).** A failed restore tries the next shorter candidate, never
+  cold; ties prefer live/chain (no upload); a FAILED attempted mount resets all stages for
+  coherence and kills live/chain candidacy while shorter saved candidates stay tryable.
+  Successful mounts never reset. Cold only after candidates are exhausted.
+- **Paired tips (F2).** One tip line holds two restorable points: the last-turn-boundary prompt
+  point (F2b: for re-rendered next turns and forked children) and the generation end (for verbatim
+  echoes), sharing one KV/MTP backing with boundary-only recurrent/indexer/boundary state.
+  The raw prompt end is never a prefix: it carries the generation header the next turn
+  re-renders as a history turn.
+- **030 checkpoint contract.** GDN/tails ride with per-layer spare keys and block cursors;
+  029-shaped payloads fail validation before any GPU mutation.
+- **K8V4 exclusion.** Hybrid KV takes no SavedState part (no capture, restore, or disk
+  offers); chain mounts there stand on checkpoint restore alone with no boundary repair.
+- **Rope identity.** Disk roots are shared across processes only under byte-identical
+  resolved rope configs, folded into the header's numeric identity.
+
+## This refactor (CELL-C)
+
+1. Restore candidate selection and the longest-first walk out of `main()` (`restore.*`,
+   `RestoreCandidate`/`RestoreResult`).
+2. Disk restore in two explicit phases: CPU-side validate (typed index disposition) and
+   GPU-side mount (typed reset disposition).
+3. `saved_state` split into the RAM store, `RootDiskCodec` (format/header/checksum) and
+   `RootDiskStore` (index/writer/trim), with `saved_state.hpp` kept as the compatibility
+   umbrella.
+4. Comment hygiene: invariant rationale stays in code; history lives here.
+5. Serve side: `CacheProtocolClient` extracted from `StrataEngine` (Muse-2; same wire
+   protocol and HTTP behaviour).
